  "body": "Part of #372. #374 refuses probing (TOUCH / RETREAT / FOUND records) by name on a machine with an inverted axis: `operation <op>: probing is not supported for an inverted axis yet`.\n\nWhy it was refused rather than translated: the Fanuc/Haas probing blocks run in the controller's frame through macro code: the G31 skip, the `#5061..` trip variables, the no-contact check against the target, the incremental G91 back-off (`DeltaX/Y/Z`), the deviation `found - expected` and the `G10 L2` work-offset write. The mirror rule would negate the target, expected point, back-off delta and `Axes[].Expected` on the inverted axis. But the #374 equivalence reader models motion only, not the macro arithmetic, so nothing would pin the translation.\n\nDone means: `invert.rs` translates TOUCH/RETREAT/FOUND for an inverted X/Y (target, expect, delta, per-axis Expected). A test interprets the posted probing blocks with a simulated trip on the inverted controller and checks that the offset written to the work-offset register is the physical correction. The refusal is lifted for Fanuc and Haas only.\n",
